      <article class="docs-content">
        <h1 class="section-title">Documentation</h1>
        
        <section id="introduction" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Architecture</h2>
          <p>Fastty is written in Rust using GPUI and the Alacritty terminal parser. It uses a low-level Paint API with strict monospace cell advance (<code>force_width</code>). Block characters (<code>U+2580..=U+259F</code>) and box-drawing lines (<code>U+2500..=U+257F</code>) use geometric synthesis to prevent hairline gaps.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="installation" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Installation</h2>
          <p>Install pre-built release binaries for your operating system:</p>
          
          <h3>macOS & Linux</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/diegoleteliers10/fasty/main/instalar.sh | bash</code></pre>
          </div>

          <h3>Windows (PowerShell)</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <pre><code>irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/diegoleteliers10/fasty/main/instalar.ps1 | iex</code></pre>
          </div>

          <h3>Build from source</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/diegoleteliers10/fasty.git
cd fasty
cargo build --release</code></pre>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="cli-usage" class="docs-section">
          <h2>CLI Usage & AI Agent Integration</h2>
          <p>Launch Fastty and automate sessions from scripts or AI coding agents:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <pre><code>fastty [OPTIONS] [-- &lt;CMD&gt;...]</code></pre>
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li><code>-d, --dir, --working-directory &lt;DIR&gt;</code>: Set starting directory.</li>
            <li><code>-t, --title &lt;TITLE&gt;</code>: Set initial tab and window title.</li>
            <li><code>-e, --exec, --command &lt;CMD...&gt;</code>: Execute command with arguments.</li>
            <li><code>-- &lt;CMD...&gt;</code>: Pass trailing command directly.</li>
            <li><code>-v, --version</code>: Print version information.</li>
            <li><code>-h, --help</code>: Print help options.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>AI Agent Example</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <pre><code>fastty --title "Dev Server" -d ~/api -e bun run dev</code></pre>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="core-features" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Core Features</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Mission Control / Tab Peek:</strong> <code>⌘⇧O</code> / <code>Ctrl+Shift+M</code> for interactive visual grid overlay of all tabs, split panes, process icons, and live buffer previews.</li>
            <li><strong>Global Multi-Tab Search:</strong> <code>⌘⇧F</code> / <code>Ctrl+Shift+F</code> powered by <code>fff-search</code> to search scrollback buffers across all active tabs simultaneously.</li>
            <li><strong>Session & Workspace Persistence:</strong> Save and restore multi-tab and split pane trees from Command Palette (<code>⌘P</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>SSH Host Manager with Mux Semantics:</strong> <code>⌘O</code> / <code>Ctrl+Shift+O</code> with environment tags (<code>#prod</code>, <code>#dev</code>, <code>#aws</code>), active connection badges, and 1-key reconnect (<code>r</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Deck Process Icons:</strong> Dynamic foreground process icons (<code>nvim</code>, <code>cargo</code>, <code>node</code>, <code>git</code>, <code>docker</code>, <code>ssh</code>) on tabs and sidebar.</li>
            <li><strong>Config Importer & Keybinding Presets:</strong> 1-click import from Ghostty, Alacritty, Kitty, tmux, and WezTerm, plus presets (<code>Default</code>, <code>Ghostty</code>, <code>tmux</code>, <code>iTerm2</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Hardware-accelerated Kitty Graphics:</strong> Full protocol support (PNG/RGBA/RGB) rendered directly via GPUI on GPU.</li>
            <li><strong>Command Palette:</strong> <code>⌘P</code> / <code>Ctrl+Shift+P</code> with fuzzy search.</li>
            <li><strong>Project Jumper:</strong> <code>⌘J</code> / <code>Ctrl+Shift+J</code> for quick directory navigation.</li>
            <li><strong>Git Worktree Switcher:</strong> <code>⌘⌥W</code> / <code>Ctrl+Alt+W</code> to switch worktrees instantly.</li>
            <li><strong>Smart Token Detection:</strong> Automatic underline and click actions for URLs, file paths, and hex colors.</li>
            <li><strong>Tab Management:</strong> Horizontal tabs or vertical tab sidebar (<code>⌘B</code>), drag tear-out into standalone windows.</li>
            <li><strong>Prompt Navigation:</strong> Jump between commands with <code>⌘⇧↑</code> and <code>⌘⇧↓</code> via semantic shell integration.</li>
            <li><strong>Synchronized Output:</strong> DEC Mode 2026 support for flicker-free TUI rendering.</li>
            <li><strong>Full IME & Latin Dead Keys:</strong> Native composition for international inputs.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="mission-control" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Mission Control & Tab Peek (⌘⇧O)</h2>
          <p>Press <code>⌘⇧O</code> (macOS) or <code>Ctrl+Shift+M</code> (Linux/Windows) to open the Mission Control grid view. Fastty renders live miniature visual snapshots of every open tab and directional split pane:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Live Buffer Snapshots:</strong> Preview active code, build output, or TUI sessions in real time.</li>
            <li><strong>Deck Process Icons:</strong> Automatically identifies foreground tools like <code>nvim</code>, <code>cargo</code>, <code>node</code>, <code>docker</code>, <code>git</code>, and <code>ssh</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Keyboard Navigation:</strong> Use arrow keys (<code>←</code>, <code>→</code>, <code>↑</code>, <code>↓</code>) or <code>H/J/K/L</code> to navigate between tab cards.</li>
            <li><strong>Instant Actions:</strong> Press <code>Enter</code> to jump to any tab, <code>D</code> or <code>X</code> to close it, and <code>T</code> or <code>N</code> to open a new tab.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="multi-tab-search" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Unified Multi-Tab Global Search (⌘⇧F)</h2>
          <p>Press <code>⌘⇧F</code> (macOS) or <code>Ctrl+Shift+F</code> (Linux/Windows) to search across the scrollback buffers of all active tabs and split panes concurrently:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Powered by fff-search:</strong> High-performance fuzzy and exact token search matching.</li>
            <li><strong>Grouped Tab Cards:</strong> Results are clustered by tab, showing process badges, tab titles, exact line numbers, and matching snippets.</li>
            <li><strong>Instant Jump:</strong> Selecting any search result with <code>Enter</code> immediately switches to that tab, activates the corresponding split pane, and scrolls directly to the matched line.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="session-persistence" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Session & Workspace Persistence</h2>
          <p>Fastty supports lightweight, zombie-proof workspace persistence stored in <code>~/.config/fastty/sessions/</code>:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Save Snapshot:</strong> Open Command Palette (<code>⌘P</code>) and select <em>"Session: Save Current Workspace Snapshot"</em> to serialize the layout, working directories, and recursive split pane trees.</li>
            <li><strong>Attach & Restore:</strong> Select <em>"Session: Attach / Restore Last Workspace"</em> to reconstruct all tabs and panes in one click.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="ssh-manager" class="docs-section">
          <h2>SSH Host Manager with Mux Semantics (⌘O)</h2>
          <p>Press <code>⌘O</code> (macOS) or <code>Ctrl+Shift+O</code> (Linux/Windows) to browse and connect to remote hosts defined in <code>~/.ssh/config</code>:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Environment Tags:</strong> Automatically tags hosts (<code>#prod</code>, <code>#dev</code>, <code>#aws</code>, <code>#vps</code>, <code>#homelab</code>) or reads custom comments like <code># tag: staging</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Active Session Badges:</strong> Displays a green <code>● Active</code> badge for hosts currently connected in an open tab.</li>
            <li><strong>Resilient Keepalive:</strong> Built-in TCP keepalive (<code>ServerAliveInterval=15</code>, <code>ServerAliveCountMax=3</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>1-Key Reconnection:</strong> If the connection drops or the network changes, Fastty preserves the buffer and displays an interactive prompt to reconnect instantly with <kbd>r</kbd>.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="split-panes" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Split Panes</h2>
          <p>Divide any tab into multiple terminal panes:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Split Right:</strong> <code>⌘D</code> (macOS) / <code>Ctrl+Shift+E</code> (Linux/Windows)</li>
            <li><strong>Split Down:</strong> <code>⌘⇧D</code> (macOS) / <code>Ctrl+Shift+D</code> (Linux/Windows)</li>
            <li><strong>Navigate Panes:</strong> <code>⌘⌥Left / Right / Up / Down</code> (macOS) / <code>Alt+Left / Right / Up / Down</code> (Linux/Windows)</li>
            <li><strong>Close Active Pane:</strong> <code>⌘W</code> (macOS) / <code>Ctrl+Shift+W</code> (Linux/Windows)</li>
            <li><strong>Close Entire Tab:</strong> <code>⌘⇧W</code> (macOS) / <code>Ctrl+Shift+Q</code> (Linux/Windows)</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="config-importer" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Config Importer & Keybinding Presets</h2>
          <p>In the Settings Window (<code>⌘,</code>), Fastty detects existing configurations and offers 1-click adoption:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Supported Sources:</strong> Ghostty, Alacritty, Kitty, tmux (<code>~/.tmux.conf</code>), and WezTerm.</li>
            <li><strong>Keybinding Presets:</strong> Switch dynamically between <code>Default</code>, <code>Ghostty</code>, <code>tmux</code>, and <code>iTerm2</code> shortcut profiles.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="kitty-graphics" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Kitty Graphics Protocol</h2>
          <p>Fastty natively supports the Kitty Graphics protocol (<code>\x1b_G...</code>):</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>GPU-Accelerated Rendering:</strong> Decodes and displays PNG, RGBA32, and RGB24 graphics directly in the terminal cell grid via GPUI and Metal/Vulkan.</li>
            <li><strong>Scroll & Viewport Aware:</strong> Inline images anchor to terminal rows and scroll smoothly with terminal history.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="widgets" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Bottombar Widgets</h2>
          <p>Fastty includes an extensible status bar with live widgets:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>git</code>: Active git branch and dirty status.</li>
            <li><code>git-actions</code>: Status of GitHub Actions runs.</li>
            <li><code>git-prs</code>: Active open Pull Requests count.</li>
            <li><code>git-sync</code>: Ahead and behind commit counter.</li>
            <li><code>kube</code>: Active Kubernetes context and namespace.</li>
            <li><code>aws</code>: Current AWS profile and region.</li>
            <li><code>time</code>: Clock with configurable format and timezone.</li>
            <li><code>command</code>: Custom shell command output with optional <code>on_click</code> handler.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="snippets" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Snippets System</h2>
          <p>Fastty expands snippets in place when you press <code>Tab</code> at the prompt. Snippets are stored in <code>~/.config/fastty/snippets.toml</code> and reload automatically on save.</p>
          <p>Placeholders support jump indices and default values:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>$1, $2, ...</code>: Jump markers.</li>
            <li><code>$&#123;1:default&#125;</code>: Placeholder with default text.</li>
            <li><code>$0</code>: Final cursor destination.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="code-block">
            <pre><code>[snippet]
gst = "git status -sb"
gco = "git checkout $1"
gcm = "git commit -m \"$&#123;1:commit message&#125;\""
pr = "gh pr create --title \"$&#123;1:title&#125;\" --body \"$&#123;2:body&#125;\""</code></pre>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="configuration" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Configuration Guide</h2>
          <p>Fastty searches for configuration in this order:</p>
          <ol>
            <li><code>./fastty.toml</code> (Current directory, portable mode)</li>
            <li><code>/etc/fastty/fastty.toml</code> (System-wide)</li>
            <li><code>~/.config/fastty/fastty.toml</code> (macOS/Linux user config) or <code>%APPDATA%\fastty\config\fastty.toml</code> (Windows)</li>
          </ol>
          <div class="code-block">
            <pre><code>theme = "default"
opacity = 1.0
scrollback = 10000
session_restore = true
copy_on_select = false
notify_on_command_finish = true
tab_layout = "horizontal" # or "vertical"
option_as_meta = false    # true treats Option key as Alt (macOS)

[font]
family = "monospace"
size = 14.0
weight = 400.0
ligatures = true

[cursor]
shape = "beam" # "beam", "block", "underline", or "hollow_block"
blink = true

[bottombar]
widgets = [
  &#123; type = "git", align = "left", interval_ms = 1000 &#125;,
  &#123; type = "kube", align = "left" &#125;,
  &#123; type = "aws", align = "left" &#125;,
  &#123; type = "command", name = "node", command = "node -v", align = "right" &#125;,
  &#123; type = "time", align = "right", format = "%H:%M:%S" &#125;
]

[keybindings]
"super+d" = "SplitRight"
"super+shift+d" = "SplitDown"</code></pre>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="custom-themes" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Custom Themes</h2>
          <p>Add custom themes as JSON files into <code>~/.config/fastty/themes/&lt;name&gt;.json</code>. Each theme defines 18 hex color slots:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <pre><code>&#123;
  "background": "#080808",
  "foreground": "#e5e2e1",
  "black": "#1c1b1b",
  "red": "#ff5555",
  "green": "#50fa7b",
  "yellow": "#f1fa8c",
  "blue": "#bd93f9",
  "magenta": "#ff79c6",
  "cyan": "#8be9fd",
  "white": "#bfbfbf",
  "bright_black": "#4d4d4d",
  "bright_red": "#ff6e6e",
  "bright_green": "#69ff94",
  "bright_yellow": "#ffffa5",
  "bright_blue": "#d6acff",
  "bright_magenta": "#ff92df",
  "bright_cyan": "#a4ffff",
  "bright_white": "#ffffff"
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>
        </section>

